	icon: "gtceu:lv_sodium_battery"
	id: "1F2D08F4FEF1CEDC"
	order_index: 2
	quest_links: [ ]
	quests: [
		{
			description: [
				"GregTech's power system is much less simple than that of other tech mods."
				""
				"GregTech's power unit is EU, which is different from the FE used by other modules."
				""
				"The EU mechanism is not similar to real-world electricity:"
				"Power = voltage x current"
				"Energy = Power x Time"
				"Resistance is modeled as cable loss at GregTech"
				""
				"GregTech is defined as follows:"
				"- EU is the unit of energy."
				"- EU/t is power."
				"- A (ampere) is the current."
				"- V (Volt) is the voltage, called LV, MV, HV in the game... because they are values ​​related to gameplay (technically: LV = 32V = 32EU/t/A)."
			]
			icon: "gtceu:lv_battery_buffer_4x"
			id: "7F97BED1B9552E5E"
			rewards: [{
				id: "21A127B9A78F381C"
				item: "gtceu:cupronickel_credit"
				type: "item"
			}]
			tasks: [{
				id: "7B797503EA800D59"
				title: "Basic settings"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			x: -3.0d
			y: -2.5d
		}
		{
			dependency_requirement: "one_completed"
			description: [
				"At GregTech, electricity is transmitted in “packets”. The size of each package is equivalent to its voltage level."
				""
				"Taking the LV packet as an example, this “package” will carry 32 EU, several blocks are capable of generating these EU packets, and the packet will only be generated when the destination can be reached."
				""
				"Every tick (1/20th of a second or 0.05 seconds), the EU “packet” attempts to transfer from the energy producer to the consumer."
				""
				"These “packages” have two parameters: the voltage level (V) determined by the producer rating, and the current (A), which determines how much energy can actually be transmitted."
				""
				"Power is transferred only when the complete “package” of amplifiers can be received. You may notice that your machines are a little below full UE capability - they will only accept UE if they are missing at least 1A of input voltage."
				""
				"If a machine receives a voltage greater than its rated voltage, it will explode, but any excess current will have no adverse effects because the machine draws only the amount required."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Machine explosions would normally also destroy terrain, but this feature is disabled in this package."
				""
				"In short, energy is transmitted in the form of “packets”, which are 32EU for BT, 128EU for MT... and so on. Due to cable loss, the actual power received by the machine may be less than the power sent."
				""
				"The machine's power input is limited by voltage and current, therefore an MV machine connected to a LV line with an input current of 1A will never accept more than 32EU/t."
				""
				"You can still run an MT machine on the BT line, but only if the recipe power is low enough, or if you have a medium voltage battery in the machine's charging slot, the machine will only accept 1A when idle, so the battery will charge at the maximum rate of 32EU/t."
			]
			icon: "gtceu:lv_transformer_1a"
			id: "0CC922B821305906"
			rewards: [{
				id: "6AACFA4A99B6EF47"
				item: "gtceu:cupronickel_credit"
				type: "item"
			}]
			tasks: [{
				id: "34D8E6B118290930"
				title: "energy transfer"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			x: -1.0d
			y: -2.5d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"EU transmission is via directly connected wires or cables."
				""
				"Wires are a bad choice because they can cause shocks and have high wire loss, so you need to use an insulated cable."
				""
				"Line loss means you need to move your machine closer to the generator, but this only becomes a problem early in the game."
				""
				"GregTech cable loss means that the transmission of UE packets from each cable block reduces its stored EU."
				""
				"For example, if the wire loss of a tin cable is 1, for a 4 meter cable connected to a basic internal combustion engine, the voltage at the end is only 28 EU/t, which is lower than the 30 EU/t of the average power of the low voltage machine. Therefore, a running machine may trip after a few seconds."
				""
				"But there is no need to worry here, if you read the mission statement, you will find that there are cheap superconductors in the early stage and wireless in the later stage, thus completely avoiding this problem."
			]
			icon: "gtceu:tin_single_cable"
			id: "4A7E19EF14D3C072"
			rewards: [{
				id: "0742E14D9F82B5DA"
				item: "gtceu:cupronickel_credit"
				type: "item"
			}]
			tasks: [{
				id: "6C551BD24A83AB3F"
				title: "Cable broadcast"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			x: 1.0d
			y: -2.5d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"At GregTech, each small generator produces a voltage level of 1A, but here the output current of the small generators is greatly increased."
				""
				"If a machine demands 32EU/t, a “packet” of 32EU will be sent every tick."
				""
				"A 4-cell BT battery box can produce 4 amps of LV (128EU/t)."
				""
				"The generic machine is set to draw 2 amps, other machines have specific amp inputs, which are described in their tooltips."
				""
				"Trying to carry more amps than the limit will burn out your cables."
				""
				"Ampere only consumes through a cable connected directly to the producer and the consumer, and only consumes when the consumer is working."
				""
				"This means you can safely reduce the thickness of cables in certain locations."
			]
			icon: "gtceu:lv_diode"
			id: "4F7A3702787F86A7"
			rewards: [{
				id: "12DB6E7A8A385246"
				item: "gtceu:cupronickel_credit"
				type: "item"
			}]
			tasks: [{
				id: "007D09C6CE7CB00B"
				title: "atual"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			x: 3.0d
			y: -2.5d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"Overclocking is a mechanism that occurs when you try to run a recipe on a machine with greater power than the recipe itself, the recipe will consume more energy, but the recipe time will be reduced according to the level of your overclock."
				""
				"Some machines have a side menu to set the maximum voltage level you can overclock to. Click here to browse all available voltages and select a threshold."
				""
				"One overclock is allowed for every four times the power supplied above the recipe power. Each overclock means: 2x revenue speed, 4x power consumption, 2x total power cost, called &b&rlossy overclock. Most machines use lossy overclocking."
				""
				"However, ULV formulas (even 2EU/t grinder formulas) will not be overclocked on low voltage machines, so they will only use LV level electrical power when reaching MV (grinder formulas generally use 32EU/t only when HV is achieved)."
				""
				"The corresponding concept is &d&rlossless overclocking, 4x revenue speed, 4x power consumption, 1x total power cost."
			]
			icon: "minecraft:clock"
			id: "5535934109A12B5D"
			rewards: [{
				id: "31ED6CE96AA0C0E8"
				item: "gtceu:cupronickel_credit"
				type: "item"
			}]
			tasks: [{
				id: "4DB7B7FC0312D572"
				title: "Overclock"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			x: 5.0d
			y: -2.5d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"Obviously, voltages can be converted between voltages using a transformer. The transformer can only convert between two adjacent voltage levels, with boost and buck modes. In boost mode, 4x voltage and current will be converted to a higher voltage and 1x current, and vice versa in buck mode."
				""
				"There are four types of transformers: common, advanced, high-current and high-energy transformers. The common transformer is 1A<-->4A, the advanced transformer is 2A<-->8A, the high current transformer is 4A<-->16A and the high energy transformer is 16A<-->64A. The red side of the transformer corresponds to low voltage and the green side corresponds to high voltage."
				""
				"The active transformer of the multiblock machine unlocked in the LuV stage can support the conversion between any voltage and any current, automatically step up/down the voltage, and can replace all common transformers in high voltage and high current environments in the middle and later stages."
				""
				"But the real purpose of the asset is to double the laser."
			]
			icon: "gtceu:active_transformer"
			id: "010CF028448C17A9"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7C3F436CBD1BBB13"
				item: "gtceu:cupronickel_credit"
				type: "item"
			}]
			tasks: [{
				id: "311562AB006A065E"
				title: "transformador"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			x: 7.0d
			y: -2.5d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"The wireless network has been established from the moment you enter the file, and has unlimited capacity &d&r, &bwithout loss of energy &r, and even &6can transmit energy across latitudes &r"
				""
				"It can interface with the wireless network through the wireless power cover plate, wireless energy/power compartment, wireless laser target/source compartment, wireless power interface and power generation array"
				""
				"Wireless power monitor can monitor the specifics of wireless networks"
			]
			icon: "gtmthings:wireless_energy_monitor"
			id: "1D4874CA93B567A3"
